{"nodes": [{"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_meta_learning_decision", "label": "Meta-Learning Algorithm Decision and Schedule Assessment", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answers the two client deliverables: which meta-learning algorithm, and whether it fits the remaining fifteen working days."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_anil", "label": "ANIL (MAML Restricted to the Adapter, Exact Second-Order)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen for train-test consistency: the Ebola protocol is freeze trunk, fit adapter, score once, and ANIL's meta-objective is exactly that procedure differentiated, whereas full-network MAML optimises for an inner loop we never run. A small inner loop also makes the Hessian-vector product cheap enough for true second-order."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_reptile_exclusion", "label": "Reptile Excluded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Its outer update is the difference between adapted and initial parameters, so an adapter-only inner loop leaves the trunk difference identically zero and the trunk never trains; the later corrected reason is that it carries no support/query meta-objective and so cannot give the controlled comparison the client asked for."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_protonet_exclusion", "label": "ProtoNet Excluded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A nearest-centroid classifier over class prototypes against a continuous multi-horizon regression target; making it apply would need a non-standard prototype-regression variant that is itself an unbudgeted research contribution."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_schedule_answer_no", "label": "Schedule Answer: No for the Full Scope", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The blocker is dependency order, not implementation difficulty: ANIL sits upstream of a single-shot Ebola evaluation, so it serialises Weeks 5 and 6 rather than running beside them, and meta-training replaces trunk training rather than extending it."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_compute_matching_rule", "label": "Compute-Matching Rule (Outer Steps = 91,000/(K+1))", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Holds trunk gradient evaluations constant so the existing ERM LDO runs become a valid matched ablation with no rerun, the largest single saving available; the caveat is that matched compute may leave the meta arm under-trained relative to its own convergence."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_quantile_archiving", "label": "Quantile Archiving on Every Future Run", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cheap on a new run and expensive to retrofit; it is the largest outstanding gap against the required metric set and blocks G4 entirely, so merging it into the meta-learning runs converts two jobs into one."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_domain_generalisation", "label": "Domain Generalisation Discharged Structurally", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "transfer_view() exposes only the four core channels, static covariates C are withheld from the shared encoder and the influenza self-loop convention was harmonised, each because it is a feature from which the encoder could infer which disease it is looking at. That is invariance enforced in code rather than by an objective."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_film_adapter_framing", "label": "FiLM Adapter Is Not a Linear Probe (later reversed)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Offered as an accuracy correction to the client's framing, but subsequently measured false: with the trunk frozen the adapter is an exact affine read-out on frozen features, max deviation 0.0."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_rescope_options", "label": "Re-Scope Options A, B and C", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A extend by one week and protect everything; B hold 30 days and cut secondary work; C hold 30 days and run one meta direction. Cut arms, never seeds, because dropping 5 seeds to 3 pushes the t critical value from 2.78 to 4.30 and makes a positive finding harder to establish."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_dengue_to_influenza_direction", "label": "Dengue-to-Influenza as the Direction to Keep", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Episodic meta-training needs a task distribution and the meta-train side is where tasks come from: dengue gives twelve countries and 6,161 nodes, influenza gives three thin panels; the same direction also has the most headroom because influenza is where transfer fails worst."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_rigorous_negative_result", "label": "The Result We May Have to Report", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "If ANIL is also negative the cross-disease transfer claim does not survive and the contribution becomes a rigorous negative: a disease-agnostic architecture, a corrected fold structure and a meta-learning arm that was tested rather than asserted. Publishable, but not the contribution G2 marks REQUIRED."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_episode_sampler", "label": "Episode Sampler and Inner Loop", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Episodes defined below the disease level (country and rolling origin for dengue, panel and rolling origin for influenza) with support size matched to the Ebola regime, plus a smoke test asserting inner-loop-touches-adapter-only and non-zero second-order gradient to the trunk."}, {"id": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_timing_probe", "label": "200-Outer-Step Timing Probe", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Replaces an estimated 6x-11x per-step multiplier with a measurement rather than quoting a wall-clock figure that was never measured on this stack."}], "edges": [{"source": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_meta_learning_decision", "target": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_anil", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_meta_learning_decision", "target": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_schedule_answer_no", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_anil", "target": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_reptile_exclusion", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_anil", "target": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_protonet_exclusion", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_anil", "target": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_episode_sampler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "progress/decisions/Meta_Learning_Decision.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_anil", "target": "progress_decisions_meta_learning_decision_film_adapter_framing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score"